      <div class="lph-faq">
        <details open><summary>Is Leapproof legit?</summary><div><p>Fair question. If you’ve bought “leak-proof” underwear off an ad before, you’ve probably been burned. Here’s what we put in writing: you get 30 nights to test them, and if they don’t hold, we refund your whole set and you keep the pairs. You pay once, with no subscription. Shipping is free. A real person answers every email at <a href="mailto:hello@leapproof.com">hello@leapproof.com</a>. Our <a href="/policies/refund-policy">refund</a> and <a href="/policies/shipping-policy">shipping</a> policies are linked at the bottom of every page.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How much can they hold?</summary><div><p>They’re made for lighter leaks: a few drops to a small splash on a sneeze, laugh or jump. If it’s more than that, these may not be enough on their own, and a doctor or pelvic floor physical therapist is worth a chat.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>I already own period underwear. Why these?</summary><div><p>If what you have already works for your leaks, keep it. These are made for the sneeze, laugh and jump moments, they’re sized by your hips (US 0–20), and you get 30 nights to test them on your own sneeze. If they don’t hold, you get your money back and keep the pairs.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Will they feel like a diaper or show under leggings?</summary><div><p>No pad, so nothing bulky. They’re cut like regular briefs with a soft, smooth waistband. Wear them under leggings, jeans or work pants.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I pick my size?</summary><div><p>Measure around the widest part of your hips and use the <a href="#sizes">size chart</a>. Go by the number, not the letter on your other undies. Between two sizes? Pick the smaller one. Wrong size? We’ll send your new size free. Nothing to send back.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Can I wear them to train, run or sleep?</summary><div><p>Yes, you can wear them for training, a run, a big day out or overnight. They’re made for lighter leaks, so if your nights are heavier, they may not be enough on their own.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Can I wear them on my period?</summary><div><p>They’re made for lighter leaks, not as period underwear. On your period, use what you normally use.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I wash them?</summary><div><p>1. Rinse them in cold water after you take them off.<br>2. Zip them into a mesh wash bag (the Wash Bag comes free with 5 or 10 pairs) and machine wash cold (86°F / 30°C max) on a gentle cycle.<br>3. Use a mild detergent with no fabric softener, or the Wash Sheets.<br>4. Hang them to dry. No dryer, no bleach, no ironing.</p><p>Heat and softener are hard on the lining. Skip both and your pairs are made to be worn and washed again and again.</p></div></details>
